{"requirements":[{"id":"managed-inventory-worker","requirement":"Run /usr/local/bin/os-comparison-worker on node1 as a managed service named inventory-worker under the dedicated inventorysvc account.","status":"satisfied","summary":"OpenRC reports inventory-worker started and enabled in the default runlevel. The live process executes the required worker with UID 103/GID 104, matching the dedicated inventorysvc account with /sbin/nologin. After a verified reboot, the service, account, executable, and execution identity persisted and recovered correctly.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9aa0f63daa874bd0","cmd-9e8036d20c8e4b6e","cmd-fd31e9792dd441da","cmd-1ea5209c8e714967","cmd-73c9c8bccd5e45d8","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"The only unnecessary mutation was invoking the worker with --help, which actually launched an unmanaged root process because the program has no help mode. This experiment did not contribute to the final implementation; the process remained after initial cleanup attempts but was ultimately removed with kill -9 before the managed service was created. No final residue is evident. Required account/service changes remained, while temporary-file inventory, package-health output, and exposed listening ports showed no harmful executor-caused changes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-043dec1b813e4658","cmd-f8fe103ef8624cd4","cmd-6e83c288488440d4","cmd-a12bd1efc0c84c24","cmd-9aa0f63daa874bd0","global:after_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The requested managed service is fully operational under the dedicated unprivileged account. The node-restart protocol directly shows a healthy pre-restart service, reboot initiation and disruption, a changed boot identity, and complete post-restart service recovery; fixed lifecycle observations independently corroborate the boot change.","limitations":["The lifecycle failed-service probe checks systemd and is unsupported on this OpenRC-based Alpine node, so it does not independently inventory failed OpenRC services.","The restart acknowledgement is a locally emitted scheduling marker rather than a provider-generated acknowledgement, although the ensuing connection loss, changed boot ID, fixed lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service directly demonstrate that the reboot occurred."]}
